ics in  the first place is their thing that  keeps me motivated just to stay in it  and when I doubt myself or doubt the  subject that's what brings me back so  why I chose physics is that it excites  me in a way that other subjects don't so  it was really through basically TV  documentaries and online video that I  fostered an interest in physics I had  sort of no interest in my high school  physics class or the teacher or subject  matter I found it completely boring I  wasn't interested in finding the forces  something rolling down the slope what I  was interested in was reading about  theories of how I guess the universe  expands or how you can measure style  eight  and if I hadn't been exposed to those  but pretty much online video materials  then I wouldn't have been inspired by my  classwork thinking about physics is  really thinking about the most inherent  aspect of the world around us it's how  things work it's being able to look at  something in nature or a system and try  to understand the intricate parts that  that go towards how that thing happens  or why things are the way they are  having a physics perspective makes me  critical about the world around me and  also I think it allows me to find beauty  and the things around me  I've been asked if I thought doing the  math major as well as the physics one  was worth it I'd probably say if if you  if you're studying for physics don't go  out of your way to try and to try and  get math major just for the sake of it I  did it because the math courses going  forward like in second and third year of  my degree I just found them really  interesting I wanted to do them I wanted  to be exposed to things like group  theory and other sort of more abstract  ideas in this I wouldn't say you it's  definitely not necessary to go forward  and research anything else and in fact I  don't think people care what degree you  have if if you have an interest in  physics and at least the way that the  PhD scheme works in Australia is that if  you've demonstrated skill and interest  in a particular area and you're keen to  go on and pursue research and if you've  got some good grades and you're  passionate people don't really care what  the words are on your degree on your  certificate they care about who you are  and whether they think you'll make a  good researcher or a good member of  their team so I didn't need  the math major for anything I just have  it because I was interested in that  thanks for everyone who left comments or  questions on my last video about a  physics degree if you have any more  please leave them on this video or send  me a message I'd be happy to talk to you  about my experiences studying physics

